A-6 (IDENTITY-DESIGN section 9.10) -- the identity calls stop lying.

musl's five identity calls are CANNOT-FAIL by contract: each is literally
`return __syscall(SYS_x);` with no error path. Patch 0001 parks __NR_getuid /
geteuid / getgid / getegid at the 0xFFFF unimplemented-syscall sentinel, so the
sentinel's -ENOSYS was cast straight to uid_t and every Pouch program was told
its uid is 0xFFFFFFDA. Not an error it could check -- a LIE IT CANNOT DETECT.

This is a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the 0032/0033/0034/0037 family, and the reason
matters because it is why no sweep had found it. Those are an unchecked WRAPPER
call whose out-struct the caller then reads; 0037's stated method is "every
libc-internal call to a wrapper over a sentinel whose RETURN VALUE IS IGNORED".
Here the return is not ignored -- the return IS the lie -- so a sweep scoped to
ignored returns is structurally blind to it. The shape-2 sweep (parse the
patched syscall.h.in into parked vs real, then find every `return __syscall(`
on a parked number, then judge each by whether the CALLER can tell) found 9
sites; these four are them minus getppid, fcntl (dead under the sentinel) and a
futex helper whose caller consumes the value AS an error code.

The kernel has had the truthful answers all along -- SYS_GETUID=73 returns
Proc.principal_id and SYS_GETGID=74 returns Proc.primary_gid (A-1a) -- and the
NATIVE substrate already used them (libthyla-rs's t_getuid / t_getgid issue
exactly those). So the asymmetry this closes is: the native substrate told the
truth and the POSIX boundary-line lied. CL-1a wired getpid through this same
seam (SYS_thyla_getpid=72, patch 0024); this is that move for identity.

effective == real, and that is a FINDING rather than a simplification: there is
no setuid, no seteuid and no effective-uid field anywhere in the kernel, which
is invariant I-22 holding by construction (no identity carries ambient super-
authority; elevation only via the legate). So geteuid()==getuid() and
getegid()==getgid() are the TRUE answers here, not approximations of a
distinction Thylacine has not built.

RAW principal, not vivarium_map_uid's root-mapped form: SO_PEERCRED (patch
0006) and t_stat.uid are already raw, and the consumers compare against those.

getppid stays PARKED -- it is the one of the five with no kernel syscall behind
it and it has zero callers in the tree (measured, with a positive control on
getuid). Left a known lie deliberately; the options are recorded in
IDENTITY-DESIGN section 9.10 rather than decided here.

